cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use LandIntel in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "LandIntel: AI-Assisted Land Intelligence for Madhya Pradesh"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Goyal"
    given-names: "Srashti"
repository-code: "https://github.com/srashtig/LandIntel"
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-19"
abstract: >
  LandIntel is a Streamlit application that runs a geospatial + socio-economic
  analysis pipeline for a chosen site in Madhya Pradesh, India (satellite
  imagery, groundwater, terrain, hydrology, roads/rail, nearby places,
  administration/census data), then grounds an LLM in that real data for
  purpose-driven Q&A, report generation, and multi-site comparison — with no
  hand-tuned scoring formula.
keywords:
  - geospatial
  - remote-sensing
  - land-intelligence
  - google-earth-engine
  - streamlit
  - llm
  - groq
